; TITHE - title theme, option 4: BANNERS
;
; The bright one, and the 1980s PC game in it: a trumpet fanfare in D major at
; 136 BPM - a 16th is one row of TWO ticks, 109.9 ms. The major key keeps
; C natural as its other pole (a flat seventh: mixolydian, heraldic), the bass
; drives in octave eighths and a snare marches under it. A is the call and
; its answer; B goes to B minor and climbs to B above before turning home.

song banners "Banners"
groove 2
unit 16
rows 32
measure 16
voice lead trumpet
voice bass bass
voice chord strings

; --- the fanfare --------------------------------------------------------------
lead LI1 = o4 a8 r16 a16 >d4< a8 r16 a16 >f+4 | e8. f+16 e8. d16 e2< |
lead LI2 = o4 a8 r16 a16 >d4< a8 r16 a16 >a4 | a4. f+8 e4 d4< |
bass BI1 = o2 d4 r4 d4 r4 | c4 r4 c4 r4 |
bass BI2 = o2 d4 r4 d4 r4 | l8 d d d d a a a a |
chord CI1 = o3 [d f+ a]1 | [c e g]1 |
chord CI2 = o3 [d f+ a]1 | [d f+ a]1 |
drum DI1 = k4 s16 s16 s8 k4 s16 s16 s8 | k4 s16 s16 s8 s16 s16 s16 s16 s16 s16 s16 s16 |
drum DI2 = k4 s16 s16 s8 k4 s16 s16 s8 | s8 s8 s8 s8 s16 s16 s16 s16 T8 t8 |

; --- A: the call and its answer -----------------------------------------------
lead LA1 = o4 d4 f+8. a16 >d4< a4 | g4 e8. c16 e4 g4 |
lead LA2 = o4 b4 >d8. c16< b4 g4 | a2 e4 c+4 |
lead LA3 = o4 d4 f+8. a16 >d4 f+4 | e4 d8. c16 d4< g4 |
lead LA4 = o4 b4 >d4 c+4 e4 | d2. r4< |
bass BA1 = o2 l8 d d >d< d d d >d< d | c c >c< c c c >c< c |
bass BA2 = o2 l8 g g >g< g g g >g< g | a a >a< a a a >a< a |
bass BA4 = o2 l8 g g >g< g a a >a< a | d d >d< d d4 r4 |
chord CA1 = o3 [d f+ a]2 [d f+ a]2 | [c e g]2 [c e g]2 |
chord CA2 = o3 [d g b]2 [d g b]2 | [c+ e a]2 [c+ e a]2 |
chord CA4 = o3 [d g b]2 [c+ e a]2 | [d f+ a]1 |
drum DA = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 k8 s8 h8 | k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 k8 s8 h8 |
drum DA4 = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 k8 s8 h8 | s16 s16 s8 s16 s16 s8 T8 T8 t8 t8 |

; --- B: to B minor, and up ----------------------------------------------------
lead LB1 = o5 f+4. e8 d4 f+4 | g4. f+8 e4 d4 |
lead LB2 = o5 e4. d8 c+4 e4 | f+2 a4 f+4 |
lead LB3 = o5 b4. a8 f+4 d4 | e4. f+8 g4 b4 |
lead LB4 = o5 a4 g4 f+4 e4 | e4 c+4 <a4 e4 |
bass BB1 = o2 l8 b b >b< b b b >b< b | g g >g< g g g >g< g |
bass BB2 = o2 l8 a a >a< a a a >a< a | d d >d< d d d >d< d |
bass BB4 = o2 l8 e e >e< e a a >a< a | a a >a< a a a >a< a |
chord CB1 = o3 [d f+ b]2 [d f+ b]2 | [d g b]2 [d g b]2 |
chord CB2 = o3 [c+ e a]2 [c+ e a]2 | [d f+ a]2 [d f+ a]2 |
chord CB4 = o3 [e g b]2 [c+ e a]2 | [c+ e a]1 |
drum DB = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 h8 s8 h8 | k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 h8 s8 h8 |
drum DB4 = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 h8 s8 h8 | k8 h8 s8 h8 s16 s16 s16 s16 T8 t8 |

order LI1 BI1 CI1 DI1
order LI2 BI2 CI2 DI2
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 2: the loop comes back here
order LA2 BA2 CA2 DA
order LA3 BA1 CA1 DA
order LA4 BA4 CA4 DA4
order LB1 BB1 CB1 DB
order LB2 BB2 CB2 DB
order LB3 BB1 CB1 DB
order LB4 BB4 CB4 DB4
loop 2
